very explosive level of Torment followed by an intense level of introspection trying to highlight milestones that the Promethean needs to accomplish to &quot;Get it right this time.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:17:15-08:00","id":419251,"title":"","content":"Dear God in Heaven, the third tier of Unspeaking What Is Known.<br /> <br /> I thought the meanest thing I would ever see in this book would be Heart of Re, but I was wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:20:23-08:00","id":419253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419251#post419251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear God in Heaven, the third tier of Unspeaking What Is Known.<br /> <br /> I thought the meanest thing I would ever see in this book would be Heart of Re, but I was wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you need it to banish the King in Yellow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:22:43-08:00","id":419257,"title":"","content":"Somehow I think this reference to the Ochre-Masked King means more to you than to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:34:22-08:00","id":419271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419251#post419251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear God in Heaven, the third tier of Unspeaking What Is Known.<br /> <br /> I thought the meanest thing I would ever see in this book would be Heart of Re, but I was wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies in general drift between &quot;Hiding&quot; and &quot;Fuck you, I'm a God!&quot; powers.<br /> <br /> That goes in the latter category..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:34:30-08:00","id":419272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419257#post419257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow I think this reference to the Ochre-Masked King means more to you than to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy now has two &quot;totally not from the Cthulhu Mythos, guys&quot; creatures mentioned offhandedly in Utterances. The King in Yellow is a masked figure notorious for either wearing a dreadful mask or wearing no mask at all (i.e. the horror <i>is</i> his true face); he primarily acts through a play that shares his name, which drives all who see it insane and drags the area around it into an extradimensional city known as Carcosa. Ochre happens to be a yellow tone, and there's already Mythos precedent in <i>Mummy</i> through the Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Affinity, which calls the Herald of Forgotten Stars a &quot;crawling chaos&quot; (Nyarlathotep's title) and has a &quot;tall, cruel-looking man dressed as ancient royalty&quot; arrive alongside it, who matches Gnarly Nyarly's frequent depiction as a pharaoh with jet-black skin.<br /> <br /> The overall fascination with stars and things from beyond time fit the cosmic horror genre well, and these little nods to its progenitor make me giddy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:39:46-08:00","id":419280,"title":"","content":"On that note,<br /> <br /> Word-Warding Bonds is somewhat lukewarm compared to what Domination can do. Considering the leg work to get a True Name.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:44:06-08:00","id":419287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419272#post419272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy now has two &quot;totally not from the Cthulhu Mythos, guys&quot; creatures mentioned offhandedly in Utterances. The King in Yellow is a masked figure notorious for either wearing a dreadful mask or wearing no mask at all (i.e. the horror <i>is</i> his true face); he primarily acts through a play that shares his name, which drives all who see it insane and drags the area around it into an extradimensional city known as Carcosa. Ochre happens to be a yellow tone, and there's already Mythos precedent in <i>Mummy</i> through the Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Affinity, which calls the Herald of Forgotten Stars a &quot;crawling chaos&quot; (Nyarlathotep's title) and has a &quot;tall, cruel-looking man dressed as ancient royalty&quot; arrive alongside it, who matches Gnarly Nyarly's frequent depiction as a pharaoh with jet-black skin.<br /> <br /> The overall fascination with stars and things from beyond time fit the cosmic horror genre well, and these little nods to its progenitor make me giddy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. Been a while since I've read Lovecraft, forgot about that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:55:32-08:00","id":419293,"title":"","content":"Damn it I do not need this right now I have work I need to do.<br /> <br /> Downloading now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:05:00-08:00","id":419300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419293#post419293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it I do not need this right now I have work I need to do.<br /> <br /> Downloading now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me about it. I had work that needed to be done by 5 today, and I wasted 45 minutes reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:06:06-08:00","id":419301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419251#post419251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear God in Heaven, the third tier of Unspeaking What Is Known.<br /> <br /> I thought the meanest thing I would ever see in this book would be Heart of Re, but I was wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Heart of Re is still pretty mean, at least from the standpoint of &quot;This whole 'modern world' idea was nice while it lasted.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:09:21-08:00","id":419303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419272#post419272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy now has two &quot;totally not from the Cthulhu Mythos, guys&quot; creatures mentioned offhandedly in Utterances. The King in Yellow is a masked figure notorious for either wearing a dreadful mask or wearing no mask at all (i.e. the horror <i>is</i> his true face); he primarily acts through a play that shares his name, which drives all who see it insane and drags the area around it into an extradimensional city known as Carcosa. Ochre happens to be a yellow tone, and there's already Mythos precedent in <i>Mummy</i> through the Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Affinity, which calls the Herald of Forgotten Stars a &quot;crawling chaos&quot; (Nyarlathotep's title) and has a &quot;tall, cruel-looking man dressed as ancient royalty&quot; arrive alongside it, who matches Gnarly Nyarly's frequent depiction as a pharaoh with jet-black skin.<br /> <br /> The overall fascination with stars and things from beyond time fit the cosmic horror genre well, and these little nods to its progenitor make me giddy.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The King in Yellow</i> (i.e., the play) would fit in so nicely into Mummy. Sooooo nicely. It could easily be a particularly nasty Text.<br /> <br /> You know, that reminds me of a question I had...which of the temakhs (if any) would match up to stage acting? The Singer, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:17:15-08:00","id":419310,"title":"","content":"Wait, now I am confused. Mummies can be affected by true name magic?<br /> <br /> I thought they explicitly couldn't be? The rules in the very beginning seem to be a contradiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:21:52-08:00","id":419316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419310#post419310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, now I am confused. Mummies can be affected by true name magic?<br /> <br /> I thought they explicitly couldn't be? The rules in the very beginning seem to be a contradiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>True Names are held by the Judges/temakh until Apotheosis; true names still work on mummies.<br /> <br /> True Names and true names are different now, however confusingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:34:40-08:00","id":419328,"title":"","content":"I just got Lore Of The Deceived and read through it. Many, many things in this book <i>are absolutely terrifying</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419316#post419316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Names are held by the Judges/temakh until Apotheosis; true names still work on mummies.<br /> <br /> True Names and true names are different now, however confusingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I have to admit I found really underwhelming. Not a change I'm fond of. Makes the fact Mummies have sealed True Names seem.... much less impressive in terms of what that means. For it being the part of the book I was looking forward to the most, I'm surprised that was actually kind of disappointing.<br /> <br /> <i>Unspeaking What Is Known</i> though, good lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:47:27-08:00","id":419350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419328#post419328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got Lore Of The Deceived and read through it. Many, many things in this book <i>are absolutely terrifying</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This, I have to admit I found really underwhelming. Not a change I'm fond of. Makes the fact Mummies have sealed True Names seem.... much less impressive in terms of what that means. For it being the part of the book I was looking forward to the most, I'm surprised that was actually kind of disappointing.<br /> <br /> <i>Unspeaking What Is Known</i> though, good lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a real bitch learning a mummy's true name, though (I think it automatically imposes a -5 penalty on the attempt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:52:54-08:00","id":419357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419350#post419350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still a real bitch learning a mummy's true name, though (I think it automatically imposes a -5 penalty on the attempt).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but it's the spirit of the thing. It's just different from what was originally presented, and I find it a bit &quot;meh&quot; in terms of what it means for their condition and that important detail now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:57:46-08:00","id":419360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419357#post419357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, but it's the spirit of the thing. It's just different from what was originally presented, and I find it a bit &quot;meh&quot; in terms of what it means for their condition and that important detail now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look at it like this: If a mummy's True Name wasn't sealed away, then a Deceived likely could annihilate that mummy utterly and completely with the third tier of Unspeaking What is Known. Besides, it'd kind of suck if Arisen were basically completely immune to anything a Deceived could hurl at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:10:03-08:00","id":419385,"title":"","content":"Oh man. One of my players is going to be immensely smug about these mechanics. His idea for a character who changed his name at the start of ever descent in order to make learning his true name harder works perfectly. It'll be a whole month before anyone can even use that name to target him, and if he constantly works to shift his name it makes targeting him quite a bit harder (and requires a fair bit of constant effort).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:20:12-08:00","id":419404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419360#post419360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look at it like this: If a mummy's True Name wasn't sealed away, then a Deceived likely could annihilate that mummy utterly and completely with the third tier of Unspeaking What is Known. Besides, it'd kind of suck if Arisen were basically completely immune to anything a Deceived could hurl at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except True Names can't be divined at all. And come now, several very scary things the Deceived can do don't even require true names. Just given names. I wasn't particularly complaining from the perspective of it making mummies less powerful. I really liked the previous paradigm of sealing a mummy's True Name, and all it implicated. It added to their uniqueness.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the fact the true names of the Arisen can still be discerned and used in such ways, in my opinion sort of defeats the point of sealing them as was presented in the core book - allowing only the Judges to hold that kind of dominion over their Arisen servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-25-2015, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:29:07-08:00","id":419437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419360#post419360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I look at it like this: If a mummy's True Name wasn't sealed away, then a Deceived likely could annihilate that mummy utterly and completely with the third tier of Unspeaking What is Known. Besides, it'd kind of suck if Arisen were basically completely immune to anything a Deceived could hurl at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fear for Arisen with Unspeaking isn't so much the death but rather the fact that they now have to risk their souls and their cults.<br /> <br /> Should this happen mid-descent, said Arisen would have to risk their soul simply to get back, then have to rebuilt their cult from scratch. <br /> <br /> And this is after said Deceived/Arisen has plundered it for relics.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:46:33-08:00","id":419463,"title":"","content":"Speaking With the Masters Voice.......What the Christ?! /Panther<br /> <br /> Seriously, that, the Utterances, the seba. &quot;Mummy magic is fucking scary!&quot; seems to be a statement that keeps cropping up for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:48:26-08:00","id":419466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419404#post419404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except True Names can't be divined at all. And come now, several very scary things the Deceived can do don't even require true names. Just given names. I wasn't particularly complaining from the perspective of it making mummies less powerful. I really liked the previous paradigm of sealing a mummy's True Name, and all it implicated. It added to their uniqueness.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the fact the true names of the Arisen can still be discerned and used in such ways, in my opinion sort of defeats the point of sealing them as was presented in the core book - allowing only the Judges to hold that kind of dominion over their Arisen servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly see where you are coming from. The main source of information on True Names prior to this was the Lost Brush of the First Scribe (or something like that, the 5 dot Text in the core), which allows the wielder to learn a user's True Name. The mechanics for having this knowledge are, from memory, &quot;any number of story-level effects&quot;, and Lore of the Deceived seems to agree with this. True Names, capitalised, seem a lot more dangerous than true names, which merely make the target eligible for certain spells.<br /> <br /> I will admit though that I wish the writers had found a different, ahem, &quot;name&quot; for that intermediate stage between &quot;use the target's given name to target them&quot; and &quot;know their True Name to rewrite their very existence&quot;. I get the desire to have certain spells that require the wielder to research their target prior to using them, it's cool and adds a nice extra layer to the effect. That said, I'm sure they could have found a less confusing term for that design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T15:58:27-08:00","id":419482,"title":"","content":"You know, I have to wonder if the Heart of Re's wave of Sekhem is akin to that of the First Wave, ie a song.<br /> <br /> Specifically, this one:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=swDIEdqSqGk\" data-code=\"swDIEdqSqGk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/swDIEdqSqGk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:07:04-08:00","id":419499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419466#post419466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can certainly see where you are coming from. The main source of information on True Names prior to this was the Lost Brush of the First Scribe (or something like that, the 5 dot Text in the core), which allows the wielder to learn a user's True Name. The mechanics for having this knowledge are, from memory, &quot;any number of story-level effects&quot;, and Lore of the Deceived seems to agree with this. True Names, capitalised, seem a lot more dangerous than true names, which merely make the target eligible for certain spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>That relic probably only refers to true names (uncapitalized) now, given this passage from Lore Of The Deceived I already mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lore Of The Deceived, pg.3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not possible to divine a target\u2019s True Name by any known means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do echo the sentiment of your second paragraph, but for me there is a bigger problem in how this book explained that division of degrees of name. Details from previous books have also just gotten muddy or downright contradictory, in following.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:12:54-08:00","id":419507,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I'm ignoring that line. A single five dot text, lost to the ages and the product of the mad labour of one Irem's greatest artisans, being the only possible source of a True Name (capitals) is entirely in keeping with the impossible amount of power granted over the subject through its knowledge. Besides, if it does only provide knowledge of true names (lower case), that contradicts the line in the relic's description about story level effects since Lore takes pains to note that such knowledge is useless to anyone without the requisite Affinities/Utterances/Seba to make use of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:16:44-08:00","id":419512,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, far as interpretations go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:23:04-08:00","id":419517,"title":"","content":"Five dot relics should do more than make instant actions easier to perform, basically <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You could also make a decent argument that the brush isn't a &quot;known means&quot; to begin with, since it was stolen in Irem and its creator put to death. Entirely plausible that no one in the world knows of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:45:50-08:00","id":419540,"title":"","content":"I wish some of the seba powers were affinities because I would just want my mummy to have those powers, and some of those affinities in here are really, really crazy. The book is a little wordy in its descriptions but otherwise I heartily approve and am grateful. I wish it was a pay-what-you-want set-up, though, rather than completely free <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:03:29-08:00","id":419558,"title":"","content":"Some of these Seba would work better as Utterances than Affinities, and even that isn't necessarily enough. I mean, the Unshade is a nastier beastie than the Chthonic Being, and easier to summon.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing is that Zelbinnean and I have been brainstorming Seba for a while, and the idea of a tomb-generating Seba was one he had a while back. Although, if I remember right, his version only existed in Twilight and provided a safe refuge outside the physical world that even a mortal could flee to. Great minds think alike, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:06:24-08:00","id":419573,"title":"","content":"Glad y'all are liking this. Any questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:14:37-08:00","id":419584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419573#post419573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad y'all are liking this. Any questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Were you intentionally trying to make me eat my 'Heart of Re is the most terrifying thing ever' words with one of those other 5-dot Seba that <i>turns supernatural beings into mortals?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:17:12-08:00","id":419589,"title":"","content":"Hm, I can think of a few. I'd need to get home to double-check the mechanics first to query the specifics, but on a more general level:<br /> <br /> Is this true name/True Name separation a more recent change in the terminology of the game-line, or can we reliably assume that any cases in which the words have been used in prior books (Guildhalls with that one Sesha-Hebsu Affinity, and the core book with its level 5 text as discussed above) are capitalised or lower case appropriately for the mechanics described in this supplement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:21:21-08:00","id":419597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419584#post419584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Were you intentionally trying to make me eat my 'Heart of Re is the most terrifying thing ever' words with one of those other 5-dot Seba that <i>turns supernatural beings into mortals?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's so scary about letting a supernatural being who binds the seba becoming a mortal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:41:42-08:00","id":419623,"title":"","content":"Of all the things in this supplement, &quot;becomes a mortal&quot; strikes me as the warm, soft, cuddly option. After all, not too far away, there's an Affinity in which a Deceived &quot;becomes their Temakh&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T18:33:54-08:00","id":419671,"title":"","content":"All I wanna say is that it's exciting to have this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:09:55-08:00","id":419727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419597#post419597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What's so scary about letting a supernatural being who binds the seba becoming a mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>The power it must take. The story potential it brings to the table.<br /> <br /> There's a message in there, too, about what art and human creativity can allow. I am not sure if it is a positive message either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:12:28-08:00","id":419732,"title":"","content":"Well said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T19:53:05-08:00","id":419760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419727#post419727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power it must take. The story potential it brings to the table.<br /> <br /> There's a message in there, too, about what art and human creativity can allow. I am not sure if it is a positive message either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, no shortage of power in seba. What's the message you see and why do you have doubts about whether it is positive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T20:55:45-08:00","id":419784,"title":"","content":"So... about that brush?<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, looking at it, it is really quite confusing. Erudite Bastion of Perfection uses the capitalised version of True Names but the description of their effects are more in line with true names. Meanwhile, the Lost Brush of the First Scribe uses the non-capitalised terminology, but the description of its effects make it sound much more like it bestows the capitalised version. However, that becomes more complicated when you consider that it all states that it cannot be used to target Mummies, because their true names (lower case) have been sealed. Since that presumably refers to the upper case, can it be assumed that the logic carries through to all instances of &quot;true names&quot; in the relic's description?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 02-26-2015, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T00:22:15-08:00","id":419900,"title":"","content":"Well, Unspeaking What is Known has just totally changed the way I was going to incorporate True Detective into the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T03:54:31-08:00","id":420025,"title":"","content":"...and now all those fears, those care-tactics in the core-book &amp; Guildhalls about how powerful &amp; terrifying the Deceived are?<br /> <br /> Now we know them to be true.<br /> <br /> Thank you ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T06:29:27-08:00","id":420092,"title":"","content":"I was actually expecting something like Unspeaking What is Known. It's a callback to what mummies could do with Ren-Hekau magic in the very first mummy book in the OWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:37:27-08:00","id":420356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419589#post419589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I can think of a few. I'd need to get home to double-check the mechanics first to query the specifics, but on a more general level:<br /> <br /> Is this true name/True Name separation a more recent change in the terminology of the game-line, or can we reliably assume that any cases in which the words have been used in prior books (Guildhalls with that one Sesha-Hebsu Affinity, and the core book with its level 5 text as discussed above) are capitalised or lower case appropriately for the mechanics described in this supplement?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The terminology clarification came out of a conversation I had with CAS in which he simultaneously expressed interest in having Deceived able to gain extra power by stalking people to figure them out and yet wanted True Names off limits for cosmological reasons. So I split the difference. You should assume that the brush and the Scribe affinity both grab the lower case true names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:44:09-08:00","id":420368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419192#post419192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shade Hunter's Leash is my new favorite seba; is it just me, or do they have the same eyes as Anpu? One Blessed Life is awesome as well. I want to build a character around the Speaking With The Master's Voice affinity, and can only imagine how rich that character's pursuit of Apotheosis could be. Tier 3 of Unspeaking What Is Known is fucking ridiculous and I love it, and it allows the King in Yellow to hang out alongside Nyarlathotep in the Mummy-Mythos pantheon.<br /> <br /> All in all, I love this. Major props to the author for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ways of Anpu are mysterious.<br /> <br /> Which Temakh do you particularly want to see enfleshed?<br /> <br /> Do note that the Memory requirements for Apotheosis disqualify those with Speaking With The Master's Voice from attaining that freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:49:56-08:00","id":420381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419328#post419328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got Lore Of The Deceived and read through it. Many, many things in this book <i>are absolutely terrifying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the scariest for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419328#post419328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Unspeaking What Is Known</i> though, good lord.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the &quot;I like it!&quot; kind of good lord, or the &quot;Whyyyyyyyyy?!&quot; kind of good lord?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:51:27-08:00","id":420385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419463#post419463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking With the Masters Voice.......What the Christ?! /Panther<br /> <br /> Seriously, that, the Utterances, the seba. &quot;Mummy magic is fucking scary!&quot; seems to be a statement that keeps cropping up for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You think I'd go to all that effort to craft the Poet and not set him loose bodily upon the world? ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:54:20-08:00","id":420390,"title":"","content":"I have a few general Deceived questions I may as well voice here:<br /> <br /> 1) The illustrations that accompany each Temakh: I assume they are images of the spiritual appearance of each Temakh (i.e., what a Deceived who is in hennet would see chasing him or her). Is that about right? And the sahu of a Deceived looks like a mash-up of the human the Deceived used to be and the Temakh's appearance?<br /> <br /> 2) Which Temakh's purview would contain stage acting? I'm assuming the Singer, but I'm not sure about that.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm still not entirely sure I grok the scope of the artistic endeavors the Keeper emobodies. So far I've got body art (such as tattoos) and naturalistic art forms (like turning animal parts into art). Is there more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T09:58:08-08:00","id":420396,"title":"","content":"1) I think the picture by the sahu section is what the Deceived is supposed to look like normally, as in without Speaking with the Master's Voice or Blessed is the God-king. Their sahu is warped, imperfect and monstrous<br /> <br /> 3) I think he also represents spiritual enlightenment as an art form, too. As someone who practices regularly, anyway, this is how I've interpreted him and why he's my favorite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:01:02-08:00","id":420401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420356#post420356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The terminology clarification came out of a conversation I had with CAS in which he simultaneously expressed interest in having Deceived able to gain extra power by stalking people to figure them out and yet wanted True Names off limits for cosmological reasons. So I split the difference. You should assume that the brush and the Scribe affinity both grab the lower case true names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means that the Brush CAN grab a mummy's &quot;true name&quot; but not a mummy's &quot;True Name&quot; (which is still sealed away inviolably). It also means that a Deceived would kill to get the Brush. Yeah, the Deceived will suffer under two long-lasting Derangements as a result, but it's not like they are strangers to Derangements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:19:36-08:00","id":420412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420390#post420390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a few general Deceived questions I may as well voice here:<br /> <br /> 1) The illustrations that accompany each Temakh: I assume they are images of the spiritual appearance of each Temakh (i.e., what a Deceived who is in hennet would see chasing him or her). Is that about right? And the sahu of a Deceived looks like a mash-up of the human the Deceived used to be and the Temakh's appearance?<br /> <br /> 2) Which Temakh's purview would contain stage acting? I'm assuming the Singer, but I'm not sure about that.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm still not entirely sure I grok the scope of the artistic endeavors the Keeper emobodies. So far I've got body art (such as tattoos) and naturalistic art forms (like turning animal parts into art). Is there more?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) I would guess you're right, but art isn't in my purview so I can't really say. I think the sahu melding is a little more varied, generally, than just a straight up combination of the old self and that depicted image.<br /> <br /> 2) Are we talking Broadway musicals or Shakespeare?<br /> <br /> 3) Not my temakh; can't help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:20:49-08:00","id":420414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420401#post420401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which means that the Brush CAN grab a mummy's &quot;true name&quot; but not a mummy's &quot;True Name&quot; (which is still sealed away inviolably). It also means that a Deceived would kill to get the Brush. Yeah, the Deceived will suffer under two long-lasting Derangements as a result, but it's not like they are strangers to Derangements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mm hm. What's a little more crazy between friends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal","name":"Nephilpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4248_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:07:25-08:00","id":420453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420412#post420412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Are we talking Broadway musicals or Shakespeare?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shakespeare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T11:09:20-08:00","id":420456,"title":"","content":"The only thing I'm sad about in Lore of the Deceived: We still don't have rules for the Ash and Thunder Qigong or the Scheming Bride. Boo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T12:05:29-08:00","id":420524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420401#post420401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which means that the Brush CAN grab a mummy's &quot;true name&quot; but not a mummy's &quot;True Name&quot; (which is still sealed away inviolably). It also means that a Deceived would kill to get the Brush. Yeah, the Deceived will suffer under two long-lasting Derangements as a result, but it's not like they are strangers to Derangements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Brush's write-up? It explicitly states that it can't access a Mummy's true name. I... really don't think it works if you assume that all it does is give access to true names (lower case). It makes it by far one of the least impressive 5 dot relics out there, and the cost of two derangements <i>every time you use it</i> isn't even close to worth its ability to just grant what amounts to an automatic success on a single instant action. And the mechanics ascribed to it just plain don't function like they're described if you assume it's referring to true names rather than True Names.<br /> <br /> I do absolutely agree though that Erudite Bastion of Perfection should only give access to true names. Affinities make things rather mundane, but when we're discussing the absolute pinnacle of relics and considering that the brush states it can't access a Mummy's name on account of it being sealed... well, it seems clear to me that the Brush was written assuming it worked on the True Name side of the divide, rather than true names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:17:42-08:00","id":420643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420524#post420524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the Brush's write-up? It explicitly states that it can't access a Mummy's true name. I... really don't think it works if you assume that all it does is give access to true names (lower case). It makes it by far one of the least impressive 5 dot relics out there, and the cost of two derangements <i>every time you use it</i> isn't even close to worth its ability to just grant what amounts to an automatic success on a single instant action. And the mechanics ascribed to it just plain don't function like they're described if you assume it's referring to true names rather than True Names.<br /> <br /> I do absolutely agree though that Erudite Bastion of Perfection should only give access to true names. Affinities make things rather mundane, but when we're discussing the absolute pinnacle of relics and considering that the brush states it can't access a Mummy's name on account of it being sealed... well, it seems clear to me that the Brush was written assuming it worked on the True Name side of the divide, rather than true names.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brush rules were written long before the clarification on how true names/True Names work, so we shouldn't read too much into the nomenclature used in the Brush's description. What makes the most sense to me is that given the new rules we have on true names/True Names, the Brush lets you divine anyone's true name for the &quot;low low&quot; cost of two Derangements (plus the actual activation costs of the Brush). At the GM's discretion, it might also let you divine a target's True Name as well, unless the target is a mummy (although functionally I don't know how much that would matter, since the Deceived name magic we have doesn't give any added &quot;oomph&quot; if you have a target's True Name as opposed to her true name).<br /> <br /> I agree that this is arguably weak for a 5 dot relic, but given that (1) a huge chunk of name magic requires a target's true name, (2) learning a true name can be a pain in the ass, and (3) the user of the name magic is never actually sure if they have the true name or not since the roll to learn it is made in secret by the GM, I can see the value the Brush would have for Deceived (or Scribes who learn name magic). Hell, given the penalties applicable to trying to learn a mummy's true name, the Brush may be the only real solution to that problem.<br /> <br /> BTW, I could have sworn that there was a Relic that alleviated the effect of Derangements on its bearer, which could offset some of the Brush's curse. Maybe I'm just imagining that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","user":"Brian888","date":". 02-26-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:22:25-08:00","id":420669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419727#post419727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The power it must take. The story potential it brings to the table.<br /> <br /> There's a message in there, too, about what art and human creativity can allow. I am not sure if it is a positive message either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm, good point, this seba allows things that even archmasters are noted to find especially difficult with their epic magic.<br /> <br /> Makes me wonder what else those who speak the language of reality can accomplish, and how much of this are sorcerers capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T14:42:18-08:00","id":420686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420643#post420643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Brush rules were written long before the clarification on how true names/True Names work, so we shouldn't read too much into the nomenclature used in the Brush's description. What makes the most sense to me is that given the new rules we have on true names/True Names, the Brush lets you divine anyone's true name for the &quot;low low&quot; cost of two Derangements (plus the actual activation costs of the Brush). At the GM's discretion, it might also let you divine a target's True Name as well, unless the target is a mummy (although functionally I don't know how much that would matter, since the Deceived name magic we have doesn't give any added &quot;oomph&quot; if you have a target's True Name as opposed to her true name).<br /> <br /> I agree that this is arguably weak for a 5 dot relic, but given that (1) a huge chunk of name magic requires a target's true name, (2) learning a true name can be a pain in the ass, and (3) the user of the name magic is never actually sure if they have the true name or not since the roll to learn it is made in secret by the GM, I can see the value the Brush would have for Deceived (or Scribes who learn name magic). Hell, given the penalties applicable to trying to learn a mummy's true name, the Brush may be the only real solution to that problem.<br /> <br /> BTW, I could have sworn that there was a Relic that alleviated the effect of Derangements on its bearer, which could offset some of the Brush's curse. Maybe I'm just imagining that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I dunno. Lore states a Deceived that learns a True Name has complete control of making or unmaking over the subject. That's a pretty neat trick to have access to. The Brush itself states that you should rule the effects on the story level, so we're basically discussing a relic that was originally written with the idea that its effects should be above mere mechanics. If we treat it as only granting true names, that is a truly significant downgrade in power. It goes from &quot;this relic can reshape, or even create, an entire story&quot; to &quot;this relic makes it a bit easier to use certain Utterances, provided you don't mind copping some derangements&quot;. It really doesn't feel in keeping with the relic's original write-up to say that it only provides lower case true names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:05:32-08:00","id":420704,"title":"","content":"Then split the difference. If used against anyone except a mummy, the Brush gives you their True Name (hijinks ensue). Against a mummy, it can only give you her true name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T15:09:12-08:00","id":420709,"title":"","content":"That's actually an upgrade to the relic... it already specifies that you can't use it to learn a Mummy's True Name, after all. In the interests of keeping the changes as small as possible, I think I'd just use the relic as it's written and just capitalise all instances of the term &quot;true name&quot; that occur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:12:29-08:00","id":420882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brian888</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420390#post420390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Which Temakh's purview would contain stage acting? I'm assuming the Singer, but I'm not sure about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a surprisingly complicated question. Theatre as we know it is the lovechild of poetry, song, dance, and everything in between. And of course, many of those art forms are descended from religious ceremonies. For an Egyptian-like culture like the Nameless Empire, it's just as likely something akin to theatre would have been seen as a religious ritual as it would have an entertainment. Egyptians had satires, interestingly enough, right along side dramas of the gods. This is a broad definition of theatre, though. If you or I wandered into an Egyptian &quot;play&quot;, we might not really see it as theatre.<br /> <br /> Which is a very long winded way of saying, uh, all of them.<br /> <br /> Edit: That being said, I haven't read as deeply into BotD as I've wanted to yet, so there might actually be an in-universe answer to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 02-26-2015, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T17:36:20-08:00","id":420897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephilpal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=419760#post419760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, no shortage of power in seba. What's the message you see and why do you have doubts about whether it is positive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Human creativity is full of seemingly infinite potential. Human creativity does not always end in good things; I would say it often ends in very unpleasant things.<br /> <br /> This Seba is the perfect example of something that could be light and beautiful that could also easily become the trigger of great conflicts and hostilities, as well as futile quests to reclaim what was all too briefly experienced that would be worthy of classification as tragedies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:08:35-08:00","id":422324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/399980-lore-of-the-deceived?p=420897#post420897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Human creativity is full of seemingly infinite potential. Human creativity does not always end in good things; I would say it often ends in very unpleasant things.<br /> <br /> This Seba is the perfect example of something that could be light and beautiful that could also easily become the trigger of great conflicts and hostilities, as well as futile quests to reclaim what was all too briefly experienced that would be worthy of classification as tragedies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention having something that has been inhuman for so long that it has problems trying to deal with being mortal again.<br /> <br /> Kindred Elders are a prime example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T01:17:34-08:00","id":423903,"title":"","content":"Hm. My Deceived players really liked a lot of the stuff in this supplement, but one part of it made them distinctly uneasy. Unspeaking What Is Know, quite apart from making them excited, was described as a disappointment. The general consensus was that it was just plain too good, and none of them felt like taking it would make the game more enjoyable for them. To the contrary, the prevailing opinion was that the third tier was so strong it would render the game boring. After a bit of chatting, they ended up agreeing to ignore that Utterance's existence.<br /> <br /> It was a genuinely interesting discussion, and I have to say I find myself agreeing with them. From something of a lore perspective, it's fascinating to see the Deceived have access to powers on that level. But from a gameplay point of view, it does feel like Unspeaking What Is Known could have a negative impact on many elements of a game by trivialising certain kinds of conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T01:19:37-08:00","id":423905,"title":"","content":"So make it a rare Utterence, one that the Temakah consider a weapon of last resort","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T01:49:45-08:00","id":423917,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's not a problem I'm in need of suggestions to fix. The Deceived player characters are the only Deceived in my game at present, and they have collectively agreed not to touch the Utterance. The problem, insofar as it pertained to my particular game, is solved.<br /> <br /> I just thought it interesting to remark upon that Unspeaking What Is Known manages to simultaneously occupy the spots of &quot;awe-inspiring sign of might and majesty&quot; and &quot;too boring to ever actually take in a game&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: &quot;boring&quot; probably isn't the right word. Don't get me wrong, it's a very cool Utterance on a conceptual level. It's more that the feeling my group got was that it would have an overall negative impact on the game experience, should they take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 03-01-2015, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:14:33-08:00","id":423957,"title":"","content":"I totally understand that perspective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T20:29:28-08:00","id":427299,"title":"","content":"Just finished it. I love how cosmos-shaking some of these powers are! In some ways, a 5 dot seba is one you build a chronicle around. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They do what all good powers do - they change the way you look at the game. Thank you for this expansion, <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4248-nephilpal\">Nephilpal</a></b>!<br /> They should make this and supplements like it &quot;pay what you want&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}